          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A crucial ingredient in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            turns out to be a coincidence of low dimensions: subobjects are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
            morphisms.
          %p
            As discussed also at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} stuff, structure, property
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theory
            classify more general morphisms.
          %p
            When one passes all the way to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-toposes"} ∞-toposes
            %em all
            morphisms, subject to some bound on size. This is made precise in the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theory
          %p
            One way to characterize an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            is as
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable (∞,1)-category
            %li
              %p
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+colimits"} universal colimits
            %li
              %p
                such that for all sufficiently large
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                there is a
                %strong classifying object
                for the class of all
                = succeed "-compact" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This statement is originally due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Lurie HTT, theorem 6.1.6.8
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            these object classifiers are
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types+of+types"} types of types
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+category+theory+and+type+theory"} relation between category theory and type theory
          #ReflectonOnCharacterizationByObjectClassifier.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
              is a (small)
              %em self-reflection
              of the
              = succeed "-topos" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty, 1)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+types"} type of types
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} internal (∞,1)-topos
              structure. See also (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Science+of+Logic#WesenAlsReflexionInIhmSelbst"}> WdL, book 2, section 1
              ).
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            which is stable under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              \-classifier
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} terminal object
            in the sub-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} category of arrows
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\Delta^1}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            whose morphisms are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            squares in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            Explicitly, an
            = succeed "-classifier" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                          %mi Type
                        %mo ^
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi S
                      %mi Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat {S Type} \longrightarrow S Type
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %li
              %p
                such that for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi p
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{p}{\to} B
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
                square of the form
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mrow
                                  %mi S
                                  %mi Type
                                %mo ^
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi p
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo ′
                            %mtd
                              %mi S
                              %mi Type
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \widehat {S Type}
                      \\\
                      \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                      \\\
                      B &amp;\stackrel{'X'}{\longrightarrow}&amp; S Type
                      }
                      \\,.
              %p
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ′
                  %mi X
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 'X'
            may be called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em name
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+morphism"} classifying morphism
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modulating+morphism"} modulating morphism
            or the
            %em internal reflection
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p For example,
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                When
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is the class of
                %strong all monomorphisms
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "-classifier" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong subobject classifier
            %li
              %p
                When
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is the class of
                %strong all faithful morphisms
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "-classifier" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong discrete object classifier
            %li
              %p
                When
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is the class of
                %strong all morphisms
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "-classifier" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed "." do
                  %strong object classifier
            %li
              %p
                When
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                is the class of
                %strong
                  all relatively
                  = succeed "-compact" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                (for some regular cardinal
                = succeed "\u2013see" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                = succeed "-classifier" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
