                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+object+classifier"} discrete object classifier
          %h3#DetailsObjClassf Object classifier
          %p
            %strong Remark/Warning.
            The point of having
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            and hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            classified by an object in an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            may be thought of as being solely due to the fact that in a 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"}> topos
            , any object necessarily classifies a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            i.e. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%280%2C1%29-category"} (0,1)-category
            of morphisms, and the point of subobjects/monomorphisms of a given object is that they do not have
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphisms"} automorphisms
          %p
            In an
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %em all
            morphisms, in that the assignment
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
